    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d988">

                <pb facs="0767" n="691" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg691"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/7733</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Navy to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Navy Department</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 23, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In compliance with your request, the
                    Commander-in-Chief of the Pacific Fleet has been instructed, in case the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Mars</hi> has not already sailed from Mazatlan, to
                    direct the commander of the <hi rendition="#italic">Mars</hi> to confer with the
                    American Consul at Mazatlan, and to afford transportation to American citizens
                    only in case an emergency exists.</p>
                <p>Very sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Josephus Daniels</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
